# Backend Refactor and Modularization Rules

1. No functionality or API response changes.
2. Use feature-based folder structure: group by feature (auth, tasks, prayers).
3. Each feature should have its own controllers, routes, models, services, constants, and helpers.
4. Move shared middlewares and utilities to /middlewares and /utils folders.
5. Move constants like error messages, roles, configs to constants.js inside each feature.
6. Move common logic like token generation, password hashing, etc. to helpers.js inside each feature.
7. Keep controller functions small and focused — move heavy logic to service files.
8. Format all code using Prettier.
9. Clean and group imports: external libraries first, middlewares next, services/models next, then local files.
10. Use environment variables (.env) for all sensitive values.
11. Setup centralized error handling with consistent HTTP status codes.
12. Remove all unused variables and commented-out code.
